ines 41-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 78, lines 41-19"}],"maturity":"official_transcript","official_detail_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcript/2017","official_disposition_urls":[],"official_docket_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/docket/docketfiles/html/public/16-980.html","primary_docket":"16-980","revisions":[{"correction_note":"Rewritten to the concise citizen-facing editorial standard.","created_at":"2026-08-30T18:24:09.357929Z","maturity":"official_transcript","revision_number":1}],"schema_version":"1.0","sections":[{"heading":"What this case is about","paragraphs":["Ohio removes voters who do not cast ballots for two years. The A. Philip Randolph Institute claims this violates the National Voter Registration Act. The state argues the law allows this purge."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 28, lines 13-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 28, lines 13-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 23-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 23-13"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 47-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 47-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 78, lines 41-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 78, lines 41-19"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on January 10, 2018."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 11-21","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 11-21"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 81, lines 45-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 81, lines 45-47"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["Ohio wants to keep its two-year inactivity purge rule.","The A. Philip Randolph Institute wants to stop the purge of non-voters."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 28, lines 13-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 28, lines 13-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 23-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 23-13"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 47-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 47-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 78, lines 41-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 78, lines 41-19"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["Ohio argues the 2002 amendment clarified that inactivity purges are legal.","The A. Philip Randolph Institute argues the statute bans purging based on non-voting."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 28, lines 13-25","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 28, lines 13-25"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 39, lines 23-13","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 39, lines 23-13"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 4, lines 23-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 4, lines 23-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 68, lines 47-51","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 68, lines 47-51"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 78, lines 41-19","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2017/16-980_n6p1.pdf","page_label":"file page 78, lines 41-19"}]},{"heading":"What the justices asked","paragraphs":["Justice Sotomayor asked if the state needs the two-year failure to vote to use the notice.","Justice Kennedy asked if the state could rely only on specific statutory clauses."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 10,